summary:
The production change is small and follows the existing OTP pattern: `CredentialHelper.createRecoveryCodesCredential` mirrors `createOTPCredential`. Local users keep the old behaviour, because the local recovery provider is not a `CredentialInputUpdater`. I found no blocker or definite bug. All findings are minor and sit in the test fixture and test:
- the test only covers a successful login, with no rejection of a wrong code;
- the fixture's recovery credential has a null id;
- the fixture's class Javadoc still says the provider must not change;
- the flow setup carries copied test code (a typo'd alias and a pointless delay step);
- there are some whitespace-only edits.

I read the changed files in full plus `UserCredentialManager` and `RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialProvider`. I did not build or run anything.
